WEBVTT

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:35.570
Asada, the Hebrew word meaning fortress.

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:42.780
Thousands of people from throughout the world daily tour the giant cisterns,

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:46.130
the ruins of the vast storerooms, the synagogue,

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:49.890
and the palaces of this once impregnable citadel.

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:56.540
Everyone marvels at the brilliant engineering skills

00:00:56.540 --> 00:00:59.700
and immense labors that produce this unique fortification.

00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:06.060
With almost unlimited provisions and water, an army could survive up here for years.

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:13.970
And most important, there was the security of knowing that a handful of people could hold the approach against thousands.

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:29.970
The Israeli army has brought several hundred young trainees here today, and according to...

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:35.770
tradition they will be sworn in on the summit of masada reaching back nearly 2 000 years for the

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:41.770
inspirational heritage that has made the israeli soldier of today the most daring and defiant

00:01:41.770 --> 00:01:47.390
defender of freedom in the world part of their ceremony here will be the recounting of that moment

00:01:47.390 --> 00:01:54.980
in history which still echoes resoundingly today the stand of 960 hebrew men women and children

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:58.650
against the 5,000 men of the Roman 10th Legion.

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:33.960
Thank you.

00:03:56.240 --> 00:03:58.020
There is no pressure, everyone finishes their mission.

00:03:58.180 --> 00:03:59.290
Go to work.

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:12.540
young israeli soldier up here has to think back on how it all began he knows that along with so

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:17.420
much of the world the roman empire had also conquered palestine in the first century bc

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:21.860
and he knows that finally the jews had rebelled against the roman oppression

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:28.660
the soldier has been taught since childhood that it took four years the full military might have

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:29.970
Rome and...

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:35.410
hundred thousand Jewish dead before Jerusalem would fall and the Romans could

00:04:35.410 --> 00:04:44.600
claim the rebellion was at an end but he knows too that for the incredible

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:49.050
events that took place on this mountain that was only a beginning

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:00.170
Thank you.

00:06:02.360 --> 00:06:03.160
Dear God.

00:06:05.050 --> 00:06:07.270
They've broken through. They're at the temple.

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:14.360
It won't be easy, but if you keep to the back streets, we'll try to meet where we planned.

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:36.270
How are you?

00:06:37.310 --> 00:06:37.730
We're ready.

00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:41.430
Two years of starvation. Killing. This is how it ends.

00:08:42.900 --> 00:08:43.960
We're out of it now.

00:08:46.090 --> 00:08:46.510
Here!

00:08:51.970 --> 00:08:56.280
Thank God you're safe. We can't stay here. The Romans are all over the hills.

00:08:56.440 --> 00:08:58.840
I know. We'll try to reach Mossad as soon as the others do.

00:08:58.900 --> 00:08:59.640
There are no others!

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:03.480
My brother on a cross outside the Jaffa gate.

00:09:04.220 --> 00:09:05.220
His wife and daughters.

00:09:07.460 --> 00:09:09.080
There's no need to wait. Don't ask me anymore.

00:09:09.240 --> 00:09:10.360
Simon Mercura.

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:12.970
Captured. He and John of Giscata.

00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:14.500
My cousin.

00:09:15.550 --> 00:09:19.370
I'm sorry. It's finished.

00:09:23.390 --> 00:09:29.890
No, no, it's not.

00:09:30.090 --> 00:09:30.510
finished.

00:10:09.150 --> 00:10:13.400
Three years later, the men of the Roman 10th Legion,

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:18.480
their spirits nearly broken by the long and tiring years of service far from home,

00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:20.560
still occupy Palestine.

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:25.720
But Eleazar Ben-Yair and his followers, headquartered now on Masada,

00:10:26.360 --> 00:10:28.900
begin to make their presence known in the southern countryside.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:34.160
acting on Eleazar's vow that the Judean war is not yet over.

00:10:40.140 --> 00:10:45.640
Great and mystical father!

00:10:45.640 --> 00:10:47.240
Don't stop, soldier, don't stop!

00:10:47.320 --> 00:10:49.480
These thy firstfruits by rights.

00:10:49.560 --> 00:10:50.380
What do you think you're doing?

00:10:52.400 --> 00:10:55.750
We need barley, mullet, grain for the cattle.

00:10:56.570 --> 00:10:58.970
The god is just like you and me.

00:10:59.490 --> 00:10:59.970
He wants...

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:06.520
to be paid all first fruits belong to the god corporal you can be impaled for doing this

00:11:06.580 --> 00:11:13.420
whose god the jews god the only god the god moloch and you were gonna sacrifice your son

00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:20.400
all the jews we've killed and this gets left alive no for long nothing to worry about little man

00:11:37.610 --> 00:11:39.770
Nobody worships Moloch anymore, soldier.

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:55.520
Left Jericho at once, they're probably all carrying the same message.

00:11:55.680 --> 00:11:57.040
Looks like we caught him on payday.

00:11:57.600 --> 00:11:58.040
Well done.

00:12:09.820 --> 00:12:11.600
thinking that soldier was trying to help you.

00:12:13.420 --> 00:12:18.000
It's war, tell him he knows.

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:37.570
Yeah!

00:14:00.440 --> 00:14:03.350
Oh, my God.

00:14:32.810 --> 00:14:38.900
The following will be read out to all units of the 10th legion, currently on occupation duty.

00:14:40.080 --> 00:14:42.980
Officers and men of the 10th, salutation.

00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:48.690
Upon receipt of this directive, the collection of the imperial tax...

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:52.690
...will commence in an orderly fashion throughout the province of Palestine.

00:14:53.950 --> 00:14:59.980
The merchants of Damascus have agreed to exchange gold coin of the realm for fair...

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:03.940
The barter of ground grain, base metals, leather goods, etc.

00:15:05.050 --> 00:15:08.400
At the completion of the barter, the men of the tenth...

00:15:08.810 --> 00:15:12.340
will expedite the payment of the aforementioned gold coin.

00:15:12.920 --> 00:15:14.840
Under the direction of their centurions.

00:15:15.860 --> 00:15:18.190
All units, more than a hundred.

00:15:18.800 --> 00:15:21.400
Imperial tax, imperial plunder.

00:15:22.880 --> 00:15:27.160
Tekoa, Ben-Gedi, Hebron, Bethlehem, they're all the same.

00:15:27.890 --> 00:15:28.630
Course closer.

00:15:30.250 --> 00:15:31.130
It runs bigger.

00:15:32.860 --> 00:15:34.100
Does it say anything else?

00:15:36.870 --> 00:15:38.970
To conclude on a personal note,

00:15:40.140 --> 00:15:42.240
as I make ready to depart for Rome,

00:15:43.050 --> 00:15:44.810
I am bound to say that this command,

00:15:45.560 --> 00:15:46.820
arduous though it may have been,

00:15:47.680 --> 00:15:50.880
will always live in my memory as the high point of my career.

00:15:51.860 --> 00:15:55.980
The men of the Tenth Legion may be justly proud of their long and...

00:15:55.980 --> 00:15:57.120
He's not going to pull us out.

00:15:57.540 --> 00:15:59.840
And may assure themselves...

00:16:00.160 --> 00:16:02.840
that I will personally bend every effort

00:16:02.840 --> 00:16:06.340
to assure them the awards of the highest military honors.

00:16:07.830 --> 00:16:11.090
Affectionately signed and by order of...

00:16:11.630 --> 00:16:14.960
Cornelius Flavius Silva, General Commanding.

00:16:16.160 --> 00:16:17.320
Remember this batch of machines?

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:23.720
No. Final assault on Jerusalem.

00:16:24.430 --> 00:16:27.810
They should be dismantled. Might cheer up the men?

00:16:28.700 --> 00:16:29.740
Or haven't they heard the directive?

00:16:30.120 --> 00:16:31.500
Yes, just before you came.

00:16:37.280 --> 00:16:37.960
Good afternoon.

00:16:39.250 --> 00:16:40.090
Good afternoon, Domini.

00:16:40.990 --> 00:16:41.530
What's your name?

00:16:42.460 --> 00:16:42.960
Lentius, sir.

00:16:43.760 --> 00:16:44.220
What town?

00:16:45.560 --> 00:16:46.100
Town, sir.

00:16:47.880 --> 00:16:49.280
I've been here at Jericho.

00:16:49.560 --> 00:16:50.160
At home?

00:16:51.500 --> 00:16:52.200
Where were you born?

00:16:53.840 --> 00:16:54.460
Tarentum, sir.

00:16:55.030 --> 00:16:55.650
It's on the coast.

00:16:56.910 --> 00:16:57.270
Family.

00:17:01.180 --> 00:17:03.000
Half-wit. What's the matter with you?

00:17:05.140 --> 00:17:05.640
She's dead.

00:17:06.280 --> 00:17:06.680
Who's dead?

00:17:07.670 --> 00:17:09.520
Are we going home?

00:17:09.640 --> 00:17:11.160
Stand out, the man who said that!

00:17:11.870 --> 00:17:12.850
I will now count!

00:17:13.310 --> 00:17:20.600
My wife. That's who's dead.

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:28.150
Julian, dismiss the ring.

00:17:32.290 --> 00:17:57.100
Call my secretary.

00:18:02.010 --> 00:18:04.050
You will notice I haven't promised you anything.

00:18:04.550 --> 00:18:05.290
There's nothing to promise.

00:18:06.140 --> 00:18:08.580
I will recommend that they make your command here permanent.

00:18:09.360 --> 00:18:10.840
Although, why, you would want it.

00:18:11.340 --> 00:18:12.660
I want what Rome wants.

00:18:13.340 --> 00:18:15.680
Quadratus, what Rome wants now is money.

00:18:16.930 --> 00:18:17.190
Yes, sir.

00:18:17.710 --> 00:18:19.470
Well, there's money to be found here, all right.

00:18:20.220 --> 00:18:22.180
But you must give them a chance to let the crops grow,

00:18:22.260 --> 00:18:23.380
and that means keeping the peace.

00:18:23.870 --> 00:18:27.100
Can you do it with 5,000 homesick policemen?

00:18:27.220 --> 00:18:27.620
You did?

00:18:29.180 --> 00:18:29.740
So far.

00:18:31.370 --> 00:18:37.220
As for this, this bathtub is older than I am.

00:18:37.830 --> 00:18:39.450
It's been hauled over half the world.

00:18:39.630 --> 00:18:43.450
It's like part of my armour, and I'm as sick of it as I am of my armour.

00:18:43.650 --> 00:18:43.910
It's yours.

00:18:44.580 --> 00:18:45.060
Thank you, sir.

00:18:45.690 --> 00:18:45.890
Good.

00:18:46.660 --> 00:18:49.370
A copy of this now for the Emperor and one for the Senate.

00:18:50.540 --> 00:18:54.430
To Vespasian, Emperor of Rome, Pontifex, Maximus, etc.,

00:18:54.430 --> 00:18:57.050
and to the Consuls and Senators, etc., salutation.

00:18:57.170 --> 00:18:57.610
Hold me!

00:19:03.730 --> 00:19:15.760
Come here! Get off me!

00:19:16.150 --> 00:19:16.870
He came out of nowhere!

00:19:17.590 --> 00:19:21.530
Hold him! I'll get the surgeon!

00:19:21.810 --> 00:19:22.130
Not yet!

00:19:24.320 --> 00:19:29.980
It begins just like this. One man. And if he draws blood...

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:35.370
that he can take the regiment with him look through the flaps but make sure

00:19:35.370 --> 00:19:46.120
you're not seen yes they're watching

00:20:38.350 --> 00:20:57.690
Gentlemen, there is either a mutiny or there is never is, and you see fit to kill me and my officers here, you better have a candidate for emperor ready for the support of the rest of the legion in Palestine.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:08.740
You'd better be ready to march on Rome and take the chair away from Vespasian just the way he took it from Vitellius.

00:21:10.800 --> 00:21:17.890
You'd be fools, of course. Vespasian is the first decent man in the job for the last hundred years.

00:21:19.570 --> 00:21:23.620
Most of you have served under him, and all of you have sworn allegiance.

00:21:24.910 --> 00:21:27.930
The penalty, if you didn't succeed, would be crucifixion.

00:21:32.040 --> 00:21:33.940
plus loss of back pay.

00:21:37.010 --> 00:21:39.450
You stupid bastards.

00:21:40.350 --> 00:21:41.570
It's almost over!

00:21:45.400 --> 00:21:46.560
You home hoot!

00:21:55.800 --> 00:21:57.120
I take it then there's no mutiny.

00:22:00.060 --> 00:22:02.140
In that case, we have to deal with an isolated incident.

00:22:04.180 --> 00:22:07.720
A private soldier, Lentius, here, has committed a crime

00:22:07.720 --> 00:22:11.700
which demands punishment in the name of every loyal citizen present.

00:22:13.730 --> 00:22:16.150
I want this man's best friend,

00:22:16.310 --> 00:22:18.510
not his centurion or his decurion,

00:22:19.270 --> 00:22:20.740
but his best friend,

00:22:21.950 --> 00:22:24.890
to come forward and carry out that punishment at my command.

00:22:25.900 --> 00:22:29.980
Not on the count of three, but now, or you'll all see hell.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:54.220
before you see Rome again come on Lucius it'll be all right said at my command

00:23:08.920 --> 00:23:10.340
Go back to your regiments, both of you.

00:23:11.170 --> 00:23:12.470
Pray the command never comes.

00:23:14.470 --> 00:23:15.130
Still, part.

00:23:29.900 --> 00:23:29.960
Sir.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:30.320
Bye.

00:24:01.280 --> 00:24:29.970
Be helped we still frighten you Miriam not for years marriage was the cure you whimper in your sleep. It won't be take

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:31.660
the boy this time. That should please you.

00:24:32.020 --> 00:24:34.460
It pleases me that you don't need him. Otherwise,

00:24:34.540 --> 00:24:37.980
you would be taking him. Eleazar.

00:24:55.330 --> 00:24:57.050
Terrible enemy knowing me so well.

00:25:06.920 --> 00:25:28.470
My friends, we are leaving our fortress now to raid the town of Hebron.

00:25:30.480 --> 00:25:39.100
you want our blessing for this take it anything just so you go you're going too none of these

00:25:39.100 --> 00:25:45.070
manners going anywhere with you if we left them behind they just get foolish ideas about not letting

00:25:45.070 --> 00:25:50.970
us back up here perhaps not so foolish we don't give them a reason for staying eventually the

00:25:50.970 --> 00:25:56.890
romans will leave and we can come down off this cursed mountain and reunite our people again the

00:25:57.170 --> 00:25:59.670
Romans have our people to slay for them.

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:04.260
Our harvests to fill their stomachs, our money to steal, our women to rape.

00:26:05.460 --> 00:26:07.620
Why should they leave? Ever?

00:26:09.230 --> 00:26:09.470
No.

00:26:11.190 --> 00:26:14.200
Life for the Romans is very easy here.

00:26:14.840 --> 00:26:17.040
So you are going to make it difficult.

00:26:17.540 --> 00:26:21.830
Starting tonight in Hebron, these men are coming with me.

00:26:23.190 --> 00:26:29.220
If they won't come, we should have to commit an offense and kill them.

00:26:29.660 --> 00:26:29.980
As you...

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:36.760
killed in jerusalem enough we're leaving immediately why the town of hebron why not

00:26:36.760 --> 00:26:46.720
build a fleet of ships and raid the city of rome we thought that way a few years ago we might still

00:26:46.720 --> 00:26:54.070
have a temple in jerusalem now we must do what we can what can you do with a few hundred men

00:26:54.070 --> 00:26:59.960
that you couldn't when you had 20 000 we can remind them that some jews

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:08.100
are still free we can hurt them make them stop collecting taxes to the romans not collecting

00:27:08.100 --> 00:27:19.640
taxes is a very painful thing i repeat general i can give you more mandragora no you cannot give

00:27:19.640 --> 00:27:24.940
me mandragora mandragora would make me sleep for three days and i want to leave here in the morning

00:27:24.940 --> 00:27:26.900
if i may beg a favor of you

00:27:30.030 --> 00:27:33.870
I'm sure these incantations will do much to speed the healing of my wound.

00:27:33.870 --> 00:27:36.490
At the moment, I would be grateful if you revered gentlemen

00:27:36.490 --> 00:27:39.050
would read the omens for my return to Rome.

00:27:39.270 --> 00:27:40.810
We have already done so, sir.

00:27:41.150 --> 00:27:44.410
Upon sacrificing and eviscerating an unblemished male goat,

00:27:44.650 --> 00:27:47.070
we found his organs to be exceedingly healthy.

00:27:48.250 --> 00:27:50.690
Your fee will be paid. Leave now.

00:27:51.490 --> 00:27:52.010
Leave now!

00:27:56.340 --> 00:27:59.980
Healthy organs. That goat has obviously...

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:02.500
had little to do with the females in this country.

00:28:03.350 --> 00:28:03.890
What now?

00:28:04.440 --> 00:28:06.240
Normally, sir, after a night's sleep,

00:28:06.460 --> 00:28:09.510
I would draw a little blood and redress the wound.

00:28:09.930 --> 00:28:11.090
You can do that on the march tomorrow.

00:28:11.250 --> 00:28:12.590
Put a temporary dressing on it now.

00:28:13.380 --> 00:28:14.020
Where was I?

00:28:14.760 --> 00:28:15.200
Salutation.

00:28:15.860 --> 00:28:16.300
Salutation.

00:28:18.200 --> 00:28:20.980
I have the honor to report that in all sections of the province

00:28:20.980 --> 00:28:23.480
the collection of the imperial tax has begun.

00:28:23.940 --> 00:28:29.460
This collection is the first of its kind.

00:28:30.220 --> 00:28:33.580
In seven years, four months and nine days.

00:28:41.950 --> 00:28:45.890
Small and ill-organized band of fanatics who call themselves the Zealots

00:28:45.890 --> 00:28:51.170
and consisting in the main of thieves, murderers and fugitives from Roman and Jewish justice

00:28:51.170 --> 00:28:56.430
seem to have lost heart and dispersed, melting into the population.

00:28:57.860 --> 00:28:59.980
There are no longer even sporadic...

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:07.340
reports of rebellion. Thus, I can finally leave this wretched land and return to Rome with both

00:29:07.340 --> 00:29:14.530
confidence and relief. Everywhere I have traveled on this final tour, I've noticed a healthy desire

00:29:14.530 --> 00:29:23.900
for peace in the attitude of the common people of Palestine. Born in this place, don't worry,

00:29:24.380 --> 00:29:29.740
we'll get back. On this, the eve of my departure for Rome,

00:29:30.480 --> 00:29:34.480
I can and do affirm that the Judean War is over.

00:29:35.640 --> 00:29:59.840
Remember, don't waste your time fighting.

00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:00.840
burn and get away.

00:30:33.230 --> 00:30:51.480
Guard, on my order, at a dead run, now.

00:31:00.030 --> 00:31:03.300
Turn out the guard, the guard!

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:10.910
You're not dreaming, father.

00:32:11.950 --> 00:32:13.870
What have you done?

00:32:14.150 --> 00:32:15.390
What have you done?

00:32:46.510 --> 00:32:48.670
I'm sorry to wake you, sir. The garrison at Hebron has been attacked.

00:32:49.110 --> 00:32:50.630
There was a good deal of damage by fire.

00:32:51.310 --> 00:32:53.560
Many of our men were killed. Could have been bandits.

00:32:55.020 --> 00:32:56.080
Were the horses taken?

00:32:56.880 --> 00:32:57.260
No, sir.

00:33:00.570 --> 00:33:02.510
Bandits don't leave horses behind.

00:33:05.720 --> 00:33:09.000
Turn out my officers. I want a squadron of cavalry ready to move before dawn.

00:34:30.060 --> 00:34:33.120
They burned the granary only, sir. I burnt the huts.

00:34:34.280 --> 00:34:34.800
You did?

00:34:35.140 --> 00:34:38.600
Yes, sir. Every third hut, I would have burnt them all.

00:34:38.720 --> 00:34:40.700
But, of course, the men are billeted in the other two thirds.

00:34:41.390 --> 00:34:43.870
I take it you were extracting information?

00:34:44.390 --> 00:34:45.570
Well, not exactly, sir.

00:34:46.240 --> 00:34:49.960
I just felt that the act shouldn't go without some sort of retribution.

00:34:50.300 --> 00:34:54.040
And having failed miserably to collect a prime source of the Empire's tax revenue,

00:34:54.320 --> 00:34:58.500
your remedy was to dispossess and ruin the farmers who might one day replace that source.

00:35:02.010 --> 00:35:05.550
Do you mean to tell me you haven't issued an order to put every third taxpayer to the sword?

00:35:06.410 --> 00:35:07.790
Are you saving that for next time?

00:35:08.480 --> 00:35:13.380
General, these taxpayers, as you call them, are also the sons and brothers of the fanatics.

00:35:13.620 --> 00:35:15.460
They know who they are and where they're hiding.

00:35:15.760 --> 00:35:20.400
And after their houses were burnt down, no doubt they came forward and volunteered to tell you what they knew.

00:35:21.210 --> 00:35:23.050
Well, sir, it's never as simple as that.

00:35:23.390 --> 00:35:25.270
Centurion, I should have thought it was as simple as manure.

00:35:26.980 --> 00:35:29.720
Jew, here is my fist.

00:35:30.890 --> 00:35:34.300
Tell me what I want to know, and I won't hit you with it.

00:35:35.500 --> 00:35:37.620
But you can only burn a man's house down once.

00:35:38.580 --> 00:35:39.080
Confess it.

00:35:39.570 --> 00:35:42.010
You just hated to see all that fire go to waste.

00:35:46.560 --> 00:35:47.040
You're a prisoner.

00:36:01.050 --> 00:36:04.020
Cheerful boy, yours?

00:36:05.490 --> 00:36:10.070
Once. When he became a bandit, he disowned me.

00:36:10.890 --> 00:36:11.830
A bandit?

00:36:12.050 --> 00:36:15.470
He knows better. He's trying to save me from the cross.

00:36:16.100 --> 00:36:19.450
To die as a bandit has no honor, but it's quicker.

00:36:19.740 --> 00:36:21.020
And that means nothing to you?

00:36:21.080 --> 00:36:22.200
Less than nothing.

00:36:22.700 --> 00:36:26.940
And if I were hanging right side up, I'd spit in your face.

00:36:28.190 --> 00:36:29.550
Spoken like a zealot.

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:30.460
Thank you.

00:36:34.570 --> 00:36:40.360
Centurion, what's your reason for this trapeze act?

00:36:41.620 --> 00:36:42.720
Sir, to make an example.

00:36:44.220 --> 00:36:46.350
What courage and strength.

00:36:46.590 --> 00:36:50.020
I would have thought that was the last thing we want these Jews to see.

00:36:50.530 --> 00:36:52.590
I have done no more than I thought was right.

00:36:53.250 --> 00:36:55.130
You haven't had a decent word for any of it.

00:36:55.800 --> 00:36:57.600
I suggest you relieve me of my command.

00:36:57.780 --> 00:36:58.640
In fact, I insist.

00:36:58.760 --> 00:36:59.760
Calm down, boy.

00:37:00.620 --> 00:37:02.960
You must appreciate the position we're in.

00:37:03.400 --> 00:37:04.720
No advance warning.

00:37:05.020 --> 00:37:08.980
Those damn savages dropping over the walls like an army of monkeys.

00:37:09.120 --> 00:37:12.590
Shut up. I want him cut loose from that thing.

00:37:13.540 --> 00:37:17.730
Now, cut him down!

00:37:31.560 --> 00:37:32.180
What's your name?

00:37:33.380 --> 00:37:36.460
Ephraim, son of Levi. What's yours?

00:37:37.070 --> 00:37:38.930
Flavius, son of Lucianus.

00:37:39.780 --> 00:37:43.640
You're Flavius Silva. The dispatchers said you were going home.

00:37:44.510 --> 00:37:45.030
Disappointed.

00:37:45.900 --> 00:37:46.320
Flattered.

00:38:01.050 --> 00:38:03.660
They've been sighted about 400 on foot.

00:38:03.970 --> 00:38:04.290
Where?

00:38:04.530 --> 00:38:05.490
In the foothills of En Gedi.

00:38:05.710 --> 00:38:08.290
There are no more than 50 legionaries quartered in the town.

00:38:08.710 --> 00:38:09.690
In the foothills?

00:38:10.350 --> 00:38:12.530
With 400 men, what are they waiting for?

00:38:13.580 --> 00:38:14.620
The granaries untouched?

00:38:14.660 --> 00:38:15.000
Untouched.

00:38:15.590 --> 00:38:16.790
Shall I order the squadron to mount?

00:38:17.240 --> 00:38:18.500
They're lying south of the town.

00:38:19.360 --> 00:38:19.980
They'll see us coming.

00:38:20.860 --> 00:38:24.430
They'll have at least an hour's warning and time to escape.

00:38:24.980 --> 00:38:25.660
Escape where?

00:38:26.070 --> 00:38:29.320
Further south of the towns, other granaries.

00:38:31.120 --> 00:38:33.040
At the cost of all the southern revenues.

00:38:35.240 --> 00:38:40.680
A good plan! You have to wait half a year until all the crops are in.

00:38:41.550 --> 00:38:43.010
You have the news for Mengedi.

00:38:45.100 --> 00:38:46.420
Who's your commander these days?

00:38:46.580 --> 00:38:53.870
Who does he want to meet?

00:38:54.260 --> 00:38:57.480
He's made a small camp outside the town at the Oasis End Shedek.

00:38:57.950 --> 00:38:59.550
He and his officers and a few guards.

00:38:59.730 --> 00:38:59.970
How f***ed?

00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:01.150
Maybe ten.

00:39:01.880 --> 00:39:03.700
You're out of calling distance from the rest of the squadron?

00:39:03.840 --> 00:39:06.060
Of course. He wants us to know he's not afraid of us.

00:39:07.410 --> 00:39:08.310
How does he strike you?

00:39:08.810 --> 00:39:11.760
Typical. Nose in the air. Limping from a wound.

00:39:12.520 --> 00:39:13.740
Very tired.

00:39:15.680 --> 00:39:16.560
He said nothing more?

00:39:16.870 --> 00:39:19.420
Not to me. His second-in-command doesn't like the idea.

00:39:19.540 --> 00:39:20.240
That much I could see.

00:39:20.540 --> 00:39:21.260
You could see.

00:39:21.440 --> 00:39:23.160
All I know is he's taking a risk.

00:39:23.280 --> 00:39:25.660
To capture a leader is worth the risk, true or not?

00:39:25.940 --> 00:39:26.880
We can deal with that.

00:39:27.720 --> 00:39:28.320
So decide.

00:39:32.590 --> 00:39:33.310
I already have.

00:40:18.480 --> 00:40:25.670
dark to see now maybe in the morning morning now is when he'll come if he's

00:40:25.670 --> 00:40:26.530
going to come at all

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:31.800
We can't see how many he's brought with him.

00:40:33.070 --> 00:40:35.390
These aren't Britons or Gauls we're fighting,

00:40:35.470 --> 00:40:39.290
good, honest rustics who stand out in the sun like archery targets

00:40:39.290 --> 00:40:41.330
and dare you to do something about it.

00:40:42.650 --> 00:40:47.470
These are more like the Egyptians, brainy bastards without a dram of ethics.

00:41:05.850 --> 00:41:07.850
Up there, on the rocks.

00:41:10.640 --> 00:41:27.100
What is it awarded by the Senate and the Emperor of Rome?

00:41:30.000 --> 00:41:34.460
The Corona Moralis, the highest military honor bestowed on a Roman.

00:41:36.110 --> 00:41:41.140
This is the legend and device of the family known as Corneli, my family.

00:41:42.340 --> 00:41:47.100
By this standard, this medallion, and by the honor of my family,

00:41:48.000 --> 00:41:53.360
I guarantee the safe conduct and return of any and all who come here.

00:41:56.120 --> 00:41:56.620
Good enough?

00:41:58.280 --> 00:41:58.800
Good enough.

00:42:09.500 --> 00:42:11.870
I have no weapons, but see for yourselves.

00:42:40.360 --> 00:42:42.390
In here? Yes.

00:42:55.900 --> 00:42:58.420
I take it you're Eleazar, son of Yair.

00:42:58.930 --> 00:42:59.930
That's who I am.

00:43:00.120 --> 00:43:02.600
This is Marcus Quadratus, General of the Legion.

00:43:02.780 --> 00:43:05.440
Yes, I know. We all met before at Jerusalem.

00:43:06.460 --> 00:43:08.140
I was not in command in those days.

00:43:08.360 --> 00:43:10.040
You're not in command in these days, either.

00:43:10.900 --> 00:43:12.380
Let's waste as little time as possible.

00:43:13.150 --> 00:43:14.570
I haven't asked you here to negotiate.

00:43:14.570 --> 00:43:17.270
I don't negotiate with bandits, whatever they call themselves.

00:43:18.040 --> 00:43:22.500
You've been called here so that I can tell you face to face once and once only.

00:43:23.520 --> 00:43:27.820
If it takes the balance of the year or even another year on top of that one,

00:43:28.940 --> 00:43:29.980
your band will be ca-

00:43:30.030 --> 00:43:35.950
and annihilated. That is not a threat, merely a statement of fact. No matter how many granaries

00:43:35.950 --> 00:43:39.450
you burn, no matter how long you can keep the distance between the Legion and yourself,

00:43:39.630 --> 00:43:46.590
the end will be the same. Still, in all, you know a way to avoid that. One way only. Disperse now.

00:43:50.580 --> 00:43:58.580
Listen to me. I've been here for seven years. Every one of those small insignias on my standard is a

00:43:58.580 --> 00:43:59.980
representation of at least

00:44:00.000 --> 00:44:09.430
twenty thousand dead jews i have no wish to add to that record i'm sick of dead jews live jews

00:44:09.430 --> 00:44:17.330
men women and children and of your miserable unyielding country then do yourself a kindness

00:44:17.330 --> 00:44:24.350
go i was about to do just that when you made it impossible but in the rush general you would

00:44:24.350 --> 00:44:29.840
have left five thousand men behind the lesion will stay of course and we also of course

00:44:30.000 --> 00:44:39.590
to keep fighting for how long how long do you think 400 can escape 5000 that's what you want

00:44:39.590 --> 00:44:47.200
to know i won't give you a head count of our troops but 400 not even as a joke at any rate

00:44:47.200 --> 00:44:54.000
it's not my worry you want us to disperse and let your syrians turn our barley into your money

00:44:54.000 --> 00:44:59.980
we won't you tell me you will catch us and kill us i invite you

00:45:00.350 --> 00:45:11.410
try you invite me to try your country is one long and narrow graveyard already your cities are flatter

00:45:11.410 --> 00:45:16.270
than your deserts your temple has been destroyed and most of the survivors are slaves all for seven

00:45:16.270 --> 00:45:25.230
years of us trying give us our due man we know how to kill prune the orchard and the best trees

00:45:25.230 --> 00:45:28.670
have survived and not just in the south

00:45:30.000 --> 00:45:33.440
Soon enough, those in the north will give you cause to turn your back to us.

00:45:33.680 --> 00:45:34.520
Then in the west.

00:45:35.020 --> 00:45:36.700
And then you'll have to turn again and again.

00:45:36.900 --> 00:45:38.180
A war on every front.

00:45:39.700 --> 00:45:40.940
You may never get home.

00:45:43.430 --> 00:45:44.830
I was curious about you.

00:45:45.720 --> 00:45:47.480
But now the answer seems simple enough.

00:45:48.220 --> 00:45:49.040
You're insane.

00:45:50.210 --> 00:45:53.790
I'm not about to argue about insanity with a man who got his commission from Nero.

00:45:54.070 --> 00:45:58.460
I think this one is about to lose his temper.

00:46:00.000 --> 00:46:05.880
I did the same at Betsaida, foolishly charging 40 archers and letting 500 foot soldiers get away.

00:46:06.040 --> 00:46:06.960
You're a liar!

00:46:07.940 --> 00:46:18.250
I've had very few conversations with Jews that didn't end in a brawl.

00:46:19.920 --> 00:46:21.800
This conversation is now over.

00:46:21.940 --> 00:46:23.000
You have not been dismissed!

00:46:23.220 --> 00:46:25.900
Is there anything left to say?

00:46:26.040 --> 00:46:29.980
Just this. You seem to have some pathetic notion that we can't find your head.

00:46:30.000 --> 00:46:36.020
headquarters give it up we know all about masada my men are not there no but your women and children

00:46:36.020 --> 00:46:45.280
are our women and children have less to fear from you than we do they're on top of the safest

00:46:45.280 --> 00:46:53.680
fortress in the world general we both know it would take the whole legion just to keep the

00:46:53.680 --> 00:46:59.820
place surrounded and those on top can hold you off with rocks and boiling water it would mean

00:47:00.000 --> 00:47:05.890
down the 10th legion for months if not years it would cost rome 2 3 000 men and at the end

00:47:05.890 --> 00:47:15.800
supposing it came in your lifetime what would you have the final victory we've seen these coins

00:47:15.800 --> 00:47:29.820
very impressive a jewish woman at the foot of a centurion judea vanquished as long

00:47:30.000 --> 00:47:32.120
as one of us is alive

00:47:32.120 --> 00:47:35.050
and remembers how to start

00:47:35.050 --> 00:47:37.320
a fire or hold a sword.

00:47:38.460 --> 00:47:40.750
This war will go

00:47:40.750 --> 00:47:44.270
on. And if I am insane,

00:47:46.240 --> 00:47:47.360
how does that help you?

00:48:08.000 --> 00:48:10.380
I think we can safely discount most of what he says.

00:48:13.560 --> 00:48:14.520
Do you indeed.

00:48:32.970 --> 00:48:35.210
The honor of your family, wasn't it?

00:48:35.560 --> 00:48:36.840
Honor is like patience.

00:48:36.840 --> 00:48:38.020
It has limits.

00:48:39.840 --> 00:48:40.940
Spoken like a Roman.

00:49:36.680 --> 00:49:38.980
No, you wait, you watch, and you do nothing.

00:49:39.300 --> 00:49:49.120
All these wars, what was it?

00:49:49.340 --> 00:49:51.400
Well, there's his version of what he was,

00:49:51.400 --> 00:49:54.380
a humble fisherman, lover of freedom, family man.

00:49:55.920 --> 00:49:56.640
Is that a lie?

00:49:57.310 --> 00:49:58.190
Not that he was a fisherman.

00:49:58.550 --> 00:49:59.970
Where he comes from, there are a few other...

00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:06.290
ways to feed yourself that he was humble you cannot be unaware of what politicians are you

00:50:08.300 --> 00:50:14.270
call him that he comes from a long line of troublemakers cousin of that one in the cage

00:50:14.680 --> 00:50:22.240
menachem was a giant of a man with the crazy eyes of a prophet one morning six years ago

00:50:22.240 --> 00:50:27.980
eleazar and some others dressed the giant in a purple robe marched him into the temple and

00:50:27.980 --> 00:50:29.920
presented him as the new leader

00:50:30.000 --> 00:50:31.670
You mean as the king?

00:50:32.160 --> 00:50:34.690
As the messiah. There was chaos.

00:50:35.220 --> 00:50:38.000
The temple faction sent word to the Roman legion of Damascus.

00:50:38.240 --> 00:50:40.700
The legion came, the rest you were here to see for yourself.

00:50:42.390 --> 00:50:45.570
You're asking me to believe that that was the way that this rebellion began?

00:50:46.340 --> 00:50:50.840
I was part of that temple faction. I was part of that great mistake.

00:50:51.860 --> 00:50:52.300
Mistake?

00:50:53.120 --> 00:50:56.100
Asking your help, it seemed to prove what the zealots were saying.

00:50:56.470 --> 00:50:59.850
In the end, we all had to fight you, will you?

00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:00.640
Give him to us.

00:51:22.790 --> 00:51:28.210
Something obscene about a country that can be so hot in the daytime and so cold at night.

00:51:31.560 --> 00:51:32.320
Do you want some covering?

00:51:33.770 --> 00:51:35.250
Of course I want some covering.

00:51:38.400 --> 00:51:40.750
Go to bed. Leave us alone.

00:51:41.980 --> 00:51:42.460
Leave us!

00:51:44.530 --> 00:51:46.490
A messenger's just come from Ein Gedi.

00:51:46.630 --> 00:51:48.130
I have disappointing news for you.

00:51:49.440 --> 00:51:50.540
There's been no attack.

00:51:51.170 --> 00:51:51.770
Is that what you mean?

00:51:52.300 --> 00:51:55.600
Your followers don't seem too upset about your capture.

00:51:56.950 --> 00:51:57.530
They're waiting.

00:51:58.680 --> 00:51:59.240
For what?

00:51:59.610 --> 00:51:59.970
A new...

00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:02.000
That I'm dead

00:52:02.044 --> 00:52:03.764
When that comes, they will choose a new leader.

00:52:04.956 --> 00:52:08.116
He will order them down from the foothills, and then Getty will burn.

00:52:09.148 --> 00:52:10.908
Maybe we shouldn't keep them waiting.

00:52:11.644 --> 00:52:12.744
That's up to you, General.

00:52:13.852 --> 00:52:16.912
But if you can't wait to see that glow in the sky, then do it.

00:52:17.404 --> 00:52:17.864
Now.

00:52:18.780 --> 00:52:19.500
Right now.

00:52:23.068 --> 00:52:25.768
Before morning, Rome will have one granary less.

00:52:26.972 --> 00:52:29.232
Then they will move on to Wamaos or maybe Gorion.

00:52:30.190 --> 00:52:32.790
Of course, at that point, it will no longer be a concern of mine.

00:52:35.330 --> 00:52:40.000
Knight, this pretending to be indifferent to your own death

00:52:40.000 --> 00:52:41.880
is a trick you've picked up from us.

00:52:41.920 --> 00:52:44.740
I've always been good at it, and I can smell it a mile off.

00:52:45.410 --> 00:52:47.470
It's very difficult to sleep with you talking.

00:52:47.610 --> 00:52:50.090
I think your life still means something to them.

00:52:50.130 --> 00:52:51.750
I think they're offering a bargain.

00:52:51.930 --> 00:52:52.740
No better.

00:52:52.900 --> 00:52:56.540
If you send me back tomorrow, the orders would be the same.

00:52:56.580 --> 00:52:58.160
No bargain is possible.

00:53:04.316 --> 00:53:06.736
Was your idiot cousin the son of God?

00:53:08.508 --> 00:53:09.668
The giant messiah.

00:53:10.236 --> 00:53:11.156
He was my uncle.

00:53:11.580 --> 00:53:12.380
Not my cousin.

00:53:13.564 --> 00:53:14.344
And for us,

00:53:14.876 --> 00:53:16.696
The Messiah is not the Son of God.

00:53:17.628 --> 00:53:18.348
He's a leader.

00:53:18.748 --> 00:53:21.308
prophesied to deliver us from the hands of our enemies.

00:53:22.172 --> 00:53:22.732
A savior.

00:53:23.260 --> 00:53:24.260
of our people.

00:53:26.268 --> 00:53:28.268
We've had many claimants to their title.

00:53:30.990 --> 00:53:32.950
The Nazarite faction and their Christ.

00:53:33.310 --> 00:53:36.920
What's been wrong with yours?

00:53:39.020 --> 00:53:41.160
Jealousy, backbiting.

00:53:45.000 --> 00:53:47.570
I'll tell you a secret, not even near Onu.

00:53:47.810 --> 00:53:51.480
Do you want to know how to destroy the Jews?

00:53:51.800 --> 00:53:53.860
Leave them in peace.

00:53:54.160 --> 00:53:56.910
They'll be at each other's throats soon enough.

00:54:00.444 --> 00:54:01.964
But as long as we have an enemy.

00:54:03.068 --> 00:54:03.868
We are brothers.

00:54:15.932 --> 00:54:16.932
Good night.

00:55:11.100 --> 00:55:14.760
Is that my shadow, that willow twig?

00:55:17.750 --> 00:55:20.630
I was fat when I came to this country, Epos. Fat.

00:55:21.030 --> 00:55:29.300
And if I don't get out of here soon, one day there'll be no shadow at all.

00:55:36.428 --> 00:55:36.708
God!

00:56:01.596 --> 00:56:02.436
Let's go.

00:56:04.060 --> 00:56:04.900
I'll be alright.

00:56:12.476 --> 00:56:15.396
Twice you've ended the conversation before I'd finished talking.

00:56:15.676 --> 00:56:17.216
Nothing comes of talking with you.

00:56:17.628 --> 00:56:18.608
What do you expect?

00:56:19.036 --> 00:56:19.696
Just that.

00:56:20.348 --> 00:56:20.808
Nothing.

00:56:21.500 --> 00:56:22.000
Liar.

00:56:24.540 --> 00:56:26.540
You're no fanatic.

00:56:26.620 --> 00:56:29.980
But you have a hold on them somehow, even the ones who hate you.

00:56:32.556 --> 00:56:33.176
Sit down.

00:56:44.524 --> 00:56:46.524
What does it take to stop you?

00:56:51.788 --> 00:56:52.108
so

00:56:52.428 --> 00:56:54.428
we're talking.

00:56:54.668 --> 00:56:55.828
I mean, peace.

00:56:57.932 --> 00:56:59.932
What will it cost?

00:57:01.372 --> 00:57:02.572
You're serious?

00:57:05.884 --> 00:57:07.764
We want our freedom back.

00:57:08.732 --> 00:57:10.452
We want our country back.

00:57:10.752 --> 00:57:11.112
Back!

00:57:11.324 --> 00:57:12.524
When was it ever yours?

00:57:13.084 --> 00:57:14.564
He's always belonged to somebody.

00:57:14.564 --> 00:57:18.964
Babylon, Egypt, for a thousand years has been a recognised war trophy.

00:57:19.772 --> 00:57:20.812
A costly one.

00:57:21.148 --> 00:57:24.408
Yes, a curse to every army that tried to occupy it.

00:57:24.572 --> 00:57:26.452
Well, there's a new possibility for you.

00:57:27.068 --> 00:57:27.708
For Rome.

00:57:28.412 --> 00:57:29.992
Rid yourself of that curse.

00:57:30.000 --> 00:57:33.660
I spent some time in your bazaars.

00:57:34.450 --> 00:57:38.030
The man in the stall usually begins with an impossible starting price.

00:57:38.230 --> 00:57:40.910
It is understood by both parties that he will settle for less.

00:57:41.150 --> 00:57:45.060
What will you settle for?

00:57:46.300 --> 00:57:49.980
You want taxes? You want trade concessions?

00:57:50.800 --> 00:57:54.830
You want rights of way? Then you must give up something.

00:57:55.490 --> 00:57:56.250
Get to the point.

00:57:57.140 --> 00:57:59.970
Give us one tax-free year. Beginning now.

00:58:00.000 --> 00:58:06.510
Let us use the money to feed the people and rebuild the temple so that they may have a center to their lives again

00:58:06.510 --> 00:58:14.720
Next if your emperor insists on ruling Israel, let him rule it as Rome used to in the days of Herod

00:58:15.730 --> 00:58:17.860
Through a governor who is a Jew.

00:58:19.230 --> 00:58:19.630
Next.

00:58:20.100 --> 00:58:23.440
Let this governor form and maintain an army made up of Jews

00:58:23.440 --> 00:58:25.950
so that the Legion can go home,

00:58:26.920 --> 00:58:29.840
so that after a time this country can assume the status of an ally.

00:58:30.000 --> 00:58:31.170
and not a slave.

00:58:31.430 --> 00:58:33.010
You have dreams.

00:58:33.430 --> 00:58:34.270
No, dreams.

00:58:34.690 --> 00:58:37.180
That's what we'll settle for.

00:58:37.420 --> 00:58:38.830
I don't doubt it.

00:58:38.870 --> 00:58:41.250
I think your people would settle for a great deal less.

00:58:41.570 --> 00:58:43.490
Yes, but you're talking to me now.

00:58:46.790 --> 00:58:49.340
You know what I say. Makes perfect sense.

00:58:49.640 --> 00:58:55.520
Suppose I agree to take the terms back with me to Rome.

00:58:55.720 --> 00:58:56.720
What will you do?

00:58:57.920 --> 00:58:59.360
If you agree to pull your troops.

00:59:00.060 --> 00:59:04.390
north of Jericho, and leave the south unmolested.

00:59:04.570 --> 00:59:04.910
Then?

00:59:05.050 --> 00:59:07.160
Then we will go to Masada and wait.

00:59:07.340 --> 00:59:12.330
No more raids. No more granaries burnt. Now.

00:59:16.240 --> 00:59:24.160
If you truly know the bazaars, you know the moment comes when the man in the stall will go no lower not to save his life.

00:59:24.440 --> 00:59:28.320
The choice left belongs to the buyer.

00:59:28.500 --> 00:59:29.980
The buyer is...

00:59:30.000 --> 00:59:30.720
Vespasian.

00:59:32.492 --> 00:59:34.092
Will you take the terms back with you?

00:59:41.836 --> 00:59:43.836
well

00:59:44.908 --> 00:59:45.408
Does me.

00:59:57.996 --> 00:59:59.996
There's nothing in your books that say no.

01:00:00.000 --> 01:00:11.880
is i don't trust it it's one of the few things i do trust my oldest surviving friend what do you

01:00:11.880 --> 01:00:23.280
trust not me for certain you're wrong trust you after what i did at the oasis because of what

01:00:23.280 --> 01:00:27.630
you did if you'd let me go this couldn't have happened

01:00:30.060 --> 01:00:36.490
You're the first Roman I've ever seen who thought that peace might be worth more than his honor.

01:00:38.520 --> 01:00:41.960
God above the Oriental mind.

01:00:58.160 --> 01:00:59.660
Not a cavalryman, are you?

01:01:00.030 --> 01:01:00.690
I can handle him.

01:01:00.890 --> 01:01:01.230
Him?

01:01:01.960 --> 01:01:04.560
As a mayor you're up on, Solomon, not a stallion.

01:01:06.980 --> 01:01:09.340
The orders from Vespasian should be here by spring.

01:01:10.610 --> 01:01:10.930
Wait.

01:01:11.790 --> 01:01:14.630
If you ever come to Rome, I'm building a villa in Praeneste.

01:01:15.210 --> 01:01:16.650
I will never come to Rome.

01:01:17.570 --> 01:01:18.350
They all say that.

01:01:20.720 --> 01:01:20.960
Bye.

01:01:31.690 --> 01:01:34.380
Sir, the tax payment has been promised.

01:01:35.310 --> 01:01:35.890
I know.

01:01:36.550 --> 01:01:38.030
It may already be a part of the budget.

01:01:38.450 --> 01:01:39.530
You know how the Treasury works.

01:01:39.550 --> 01:01:40.370
They won't be disappointed.

01:01:40.370 --> 01:01:42.170
I'll cover it from my personal funds.

01:01:42.290 --> 01:01:43.970
The Empire and I have the same banker.

01:01:43.990 --> 01:01:45.550
It's merely a question of paperwork.

01:01:45.650 --> 01:01:46.550
It's an enormous sum.

01:01:46.590 --> 01:01:47.210
It is indeed.

01:01:47.630 --> 01:01:48.550
It's all I have.

01:01:49.810 --> 01:01:51.110
Vespasian will reimburse me.

01:01:52.020 --> 01:01:54.720
Quadratus, you understand this conversation is unofficial

01:01:54.720 --> 01:01:57.760
and, in fact, never took place.

01:01:59.000 --> 01:01:59.480
Of course.

01:02:00.480 --> 01:02:06.090
once more officially all elements of the legion to be pulled back and billeted in jericho

01:02:06.090 --> 01:02:18.800
no patrols no sorties no action of any kind except in defense and no further attempt be

01:02:18.800 --> 01:02:24.590
made to collect taxes until the new directives come through any questions none sir before you

01:02:24.590 --> 01:02:29.550
yourself return to jericho i want these burnt out huts rebuilt may i ask why sir

01:02:30.000 --> 01:02:33.630
For nothing, Quadratus, for nothing.

01:02:48.160 --> 01:02:49.200
You're going to the port? Yes.

01:02:49.640 --> 01:02:51.060
This is for no one but Musianus.

01:02:51.600 --> 01:02:53.840
Tell one of the sailors we can trust to bring it to him at his home,

01:02:53.940 --> 01:02:55.480
not at the Senate. And to add this,

01:02:55.800 --> 01:02:58.100
Silver is paying the taxes out of his own pocket.

01:02:59.320 --> 01:02:59.620
No.

01:03:01.180 --> 01:03:01.840
Hurry, you'll be missed.

01:03:15.690 --> 01:03:18.860
Sir, what about the burnt-out huts?

01:03:19.390 --> 01:03:23.380
Orders, time being, are orders.

01:03:39.850 --> 01:03:42.960
He let you go? He's a sensible man.

01:03:43.970 --> 01:03:49.340
What now? I made him a proposal for peace.

01:03:50.160 --> 01:03:53.240
He promised to take it to Rome, and we'll wait to hear Vespasian's answer.

01:03:53.680 --> 01:03:57.640
And meanwhile? Meanwhile, we tend our crops and we raise our children.

01:03:59.110 --> 01:03:59.970
Or is it the other way?

01:04:00.000 --> 01:04:03.240
With a worthless promise, he does what he couldn't do with his legion.

01:04:03.340 --> 01:04:04.120
He takes away our swords.

01:04:04.400 --> 01:04:07.220
He promised to pull his men back to Jericho.

01:04:07.420 --> 01:04:08.260
I believe him.

01:04:08.400 --> 01:04:10.060
Romans are suckled on lies.

01:04:10.240 --> 01:04:12.320
If he lied, we will know what to do.

01:04:13.250 --> 01:04:14.970
In time, we keep our word.

01:04:16.530 --> 01:04:20.120
We wait till we see what Rome has to say.

01:04:30.990 --> 01:04:45.280
riddle towered up most powerful of men mortal eyes but looked on him with envy yet in the end

01:04:45.660 --> 01:04:47.620
ruins swept over him

01:05:00.410 --> 01:05:08.590
consider his last day and let none presume on his good fortune until he

01:05:08.590 --> 01:05:27.340
find life a memory without pain you have witnessed the oedipus of

01:05:27.340 --> 01:05:29.810
sophocles a banquet for the soul

01:05:30.440 --> 01:05:33.780
Then, if the imperial palette is ready for the laxity,

01:05:34.790 --> 01:05:38.280
we'll proceed to our afterpiece.

01:05:39.050 --> 01:05:40.750
A newly commissioned dump show,

01:05:41.590 --> 01:05:45.950
as usual, unfit for the delicate sensibilities of the Vestal Virgins.

01:05:46.110 --> 01:05:49.050
With apologies and farewell to the ladies.

01:05:51.250 --> 01:05:53.010
I've heard about this pantomime.

01:05:53.300 --> 01:05:54.480
Spoiling for me, woman.

01:05:55.600 --> 01:05:56.860
Keep above the eggshells.

01:06:00.000 --> 01:06:02.600
Caesar, before our presentation.

01:06:03.290 --> 01:06:05.900
Yes, I pardon you all in advance.

01:06:30.540 --> 01:06:31.270
Ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha.

01:07:01.720 --> 01:07:03.780
Yeah, you're laughing. You understand?

01:07:18.860 --> 01:07:29.580
Sir, Flavius Silva has arrived from the seaport.

01:07:29.780 --> 01:07:29.960
He's a...

01:07:30.000 --> 01:07:31.320
at the Temple of Mars, as you ordered.

01:07:31.740 --> 01:07:32.820
He stays there outside.

01:07:33.580 --> 01:07:35.360
He speaks to no one, not even the priests.

01:08:01.340 --> 01:08:02.420
Just like the Egyptians.

01:08:31.630 --> 01:08:32.840
Ha ha ha!

01:09:01.560 --> 01:09:03.400
Masterpiece of subtlety and taste.

01:09:03.900 --> 01:09:05.400
Is the author a protégé of yours?

01:09:06.550 --> 01:09:07.970
Anonymously written, Caesar.

01:09:09.470 --> 01:09:10.590
It begins to bore me.

01:09:11.520 --> 01:09:12.460
Does it go on much longer?

01:09:13.440 --> 01:09:14.780
That remains to be seen.

01:09:31.050 --> 01:09:35.850
Welcome. I'm a poor excuse for an official reception, aren't I?

01:09:36.050 --> 01:09:37.070
Did they give you something to eat?

01:09:37.680 --> 01:09:40.640
Yes, they gave me something to eat. That was three hours ago.

01:09:41.810 --> 01:09:43.290
Would you mind telling me what all this is about?

01:09:44.090 --> 01:09:47.970
I'd love to do just that, my friend, but the Emperor's yet to tell anyone, including me.

01:09:48.740 --> 01:09:50.580
But you'll find out soon enough. I've been sent to fetch you.

01:09:54.780 --> 01:09:58.760
Judea's an awful place. It goes well with you, I take it.

01:10:00.600 --> 01:10:03.360
The gods have decided to be reasonable for a change.

01:10:03.930 --> 01:10:07.210
Hard work is reward. I don't expect it to last.

01:10:08.200 --> 01:10:09.860
Well, forgive me. We'd better talk as we walk.

01:10:11.680 --> 01:10:12.600
Vespasian, how is he?

01:10:13.160 --> 01:10:14.100
His health is excellent.

01:10:14.360 --> 01:10:17.240
We've spoken to nobody since you landed, especially about that awful place.

01:10:17.460 --> 01:10:18.740
Not even the statues.

01:10:19.240 --> 01:10:23.300
No, this way. It's shorter. I see you still limp from your wound.

01:10:29.400 --> 01:10:29.640
Come.

01:10:30.800 --> 01:10:33.420
How do you know about my wound? It wasn't mentioned in dispatches.

01:10:34.060 --> 01:10:35.680
There are dispatches. Dispatches.

01:10:36.090 --> 01:10:38.090
One thing I can tell you, the Emperor and his sons

01:10:38.450 --> 01:10:40.680
are no longer so secure as they were a year ago.

01:10:40.800 --> 01:10:42.160
There's a rival for the position.

01:10:42.380 --> 01:10:42.860
So soon?

01:10:43.920 --> 01:10:46.520
Vespasian's instructions are for you to enter the council chamber

01:10:46.520 --> 01:10:48.660
and be surprised at nothing that you see there.

01:10:48.780 --> 01:10:50.580
Friend, if I knew what was expected of me...

01:10:50.580 --> 01:10:52.240
Dead silence, friend, and a blank expression.

01:10:58.300 --> 01:10:58.880
Nice respects.

01:11:00.190 --> 01:11:03.330
General of the Army, Cornelius Flavius Silver.

01:11:03.490 --> 01:11:10.730
It is that the Privy Council paused in its work

01:11:10.730 --> 01:11:13.820
to welcome and applaud a comrade in arms.

01:11:23.980 --> 01:11:26.160
The Senate may express my surprise and delight

01:11:26.160 --> 01:11:28.780
on seeing General Silver safe and alive.

01:11:29.680 --> 01:11:29.980
May I...

01:11:30.000 --> 01:11:35.980
voice the hope that the great 10th legion is also safe you see honest you place the general at a

01:11:35.980 --> 01:11:43.520
disadvantage since none but members may speak in this chamber allow me to speak for him no legion

01:11:43.520 --> 01:11:48.060
in the world this evening is safer than the 10th now i wonder if that's because they were pulled

01:11:48.060 --> 01:11:59.980
back so far from the enemy enemy what enemy do i understand caesar that you wish

01:12:00.000 --> 01:12:05.350
to bring up the judean question now i understand that you've been burning to bring it up for weeks

01:12:05.350 --> 01:12:11.330
very well by all means museanus let us have a frank and open exchange of views i bring this

01:12:11.330 --> 01:12:17.200
up caesar simply because i am curious as to why the general found it necessary to meet there

01:12:17.200 --> 01:12:26.760
with the commander of the jewish forces and conclude a truce a truce a truce is not possible

01:12:26.760 --> 01:12:29.820
unless there is a war and there is no war in judea

01:12:30.730 --> 01:12:35.350
The general, using his judgment as a soldier, decided to show mercy to a bandit.

01:12:35.470 --> 01:12:36.970
We must all, on occasion, do that.

01:12:37.620 --> 01:12:42.050
Nevertheless, it would appear that you have allowed this excellent officer

01:12:42.050 --> 01:12:45.230
to return without having finished his job. Why?

01:12:45.830 --> 01:12:48.090
My dear, Lucianus, I thought everyone knew that.

01:12:48.230 --> 01:12:51.770
Even your own sources. Allow me to tell you, then.

01:12:52.820 --> 01:12:56.640
This excellent officer has returned to celebrate my forthcoming birthday,

01:12:56.680 --> 01:12:59.630
to have his wound looked at by some proper physicians.

01:13:00.480 --> 01:13:05.570
And once, with the approval of the Senate, he has accepted the post of Governor-General of Judea.

01:13:07.180 --> 01:13:12.060
He will return to take up that post and deal with those minor matters that seem to fill your correspondence.

01:13:13.920 --> 01:13:16.620
There are still one or two niggling questions.

01:13:17.170 --> 01:13:19.190
Niggle away, man, it's your speciality.

01:13:19.770 --> 01:13:22.310
We have been promised the resumption of tax payments.

01:13:22.310 --> 01:13:23.510
You have been promised nothing.

01:13:23.790 --> 01:13:26.890
The Roman people have been promised the revenues and the promise has been kept.

01:13:27.130 --> 01:13:29.970
But how long can General Silver continue to pay?

01:13:30.000 --> 01:13:51.130
the taxes out of his own personal funds if you will permit me i have had some experience in the

01:13:51.130 --> 01:13:59.370
area of international monetary exchange what general silver has done is this on being informed

01:14:00.060 --> 01:14:03.960
of his impending appointment, he merely notified his bankers in Rome

01:14:03.960 --> 01:14:06.220
to advance the tax revenues here.

01:14:07.760 --> 01:14:10.660
The Judean collections are mainly in Syrian currency,

01:14:10.840 --> 01:14:13.460
which the new Governor-General would find more easily

01:14:13.460 --> 01:14:16.260
dispersible for his own use in that part of the world.

01:14:16.920 --> 01:14:20.620
As a matter of fact, in saving us a 5% conversion fee,

01:14:20.880 --> 01:14:23.160
the General has done the Empire yet another service.

01:14:26.090 --> 01:14:26.690
Anything else?

01:14:27.380 --> 01:14:29.980
Caesar, this is all very impressive. What...

01:14:30.000 --> 01:14:34.740
I want to know is when can we expect the 10th legion to be free for duty elsewhere in the

01:14:34.740 --> 01:14:40.840
empire? How strong are these bandits? Where do we stand in Judea? We stand ready to bring the

01:14:40.840 --> 01:14:49.480
legion out. Well, with all due respect, next week, next month, next year, the Senate wishes to know

01:14:49.480 --> 01:14:56.010
within six months from today, the 10th legion will be free for duty on the Danube. And the

01:14:56.010 --> 01:14:59.900
emperor will say as much for the entire Senate. The

01:15:00.000 --> 01:15:02.120
The emperor will say as much before the entire country.

01:15:02.620 --> 01:15:05.360
This council begins to resemble something less dignified.

01:15:05.680 --> 01:15:08.220
For that, you have the street corners, Musianus. We're adjourned.

01:15:08.780 --> 01:15:10.220
General, please join us in the other room.

01:15:18.350 --> 01:15:19.370
Boy, we've stopped him.

01:15:19.510 --> 01:15:21.130
Oh, rubbish. We've slowed him down, that's all.

01:15:21.250 --> 01:15:22.330
Were you listening? Yes.

01:15:22.750 --> 01:15:23.110
What do you think?

01:15:23.440 --> 01:15:25.400
I think he's not strong enough. Not yet.

01:15:25.920 --> 01:15:28.560
He hasn't got the Praetorians. They're still neutral.

01:15:28.880 --> 01:15:29.760
Bloody ingrates.

01:15:31.340 --> 01:15:33.580
The impudence has been neutral after all I've done for them.

01:15:34.280 --> 01:15:37.760
Next thing you'll try will be the nomination of one of his faction as co-concerts.

01:15:37.820 --> 01:15:41.580
I agree, Caesar. I advise you not to block him. He'll only make an issue of it.

01:15:41.680 --> 01:15:42.800
Especially if he hasn't got the votes.

01:15:42.820 --> 01:15:44.660
If, we've got to be sure before we do anything.

01:15:46.840 --> 01:15:50.950
After Nero killed himself, three emperors in one year went out of that window.

01:15:51.910 --> 01:15:54.230
Largely because they couldn't judge the strength of the opposition.

01:15:55.520 --> 01:15:58.280
If Vitellius had known how shaky my support was, he'd still be here.

01:15:59.350 --> 01:15:59.970
Thanks to the new...

01:16:00.000 --> 01:16:04.300
governor general it was very nearly my turn what were you thinking of silver if that question isn't

01:16:04.300 --> 01:16:11.160
rhetorical i would like to answer it answer i was thinking that the concessions they want are a very

01:16:11.160 --> 01:16:18.280
small price to pay for peace and order and the revenues i was thinking of the good of rome my

01:16:18.280 --> 01:16:23.550
judgment in these your judgment you're a soldier you're supposed to fight not make policy with your

01:16:23.550 --> 01:16:28.810
permission i was not making policy i agreed only to bring the terms to you caesar what do they want

01:16:30.220 --> 01:16:33.850
Temple, their own governor, these things they had once.

01:16:35.220 --> 01:16:37.740
It's my belief that our strategy there has been a mistaken one.

01:16:37.820 --> 01:16:39.740
What they want is what we should have done in the first place.

01:16:41.740 --> 01:16:47.390
All right, you've answered. Maybe you're right.

01:16:48.500 --> 01:16:50.800
But the point is, we cannot grant those concessions now.

01:16:50.940 --> 01:16:51.920
You saw, you heard.

01:16:52.970 --> 01:16:56.550
It hadn't been for our friend Falco here, double-talking the Privy Council.

01:16:56.670 --> 01:16:58.170
We'd probably all be on horseback by now.

01:17:00.160 --> 01:17:00.820
I won't forget, then.

01:17:01.500 --> 01:17:02.080
Nothing, Caesar.

01:17:05.690 --> 01:17:06.370
It's too late.

01:17:07.520 --> 01:17:10.120
You can't grant concessions once you've proclaimed a victory.

01:17:10.740 --> 01:17:12.600
What's left of the opposition must be stamped out.

01:17:13.290 --> 01:17:14.950
The entire leadership brought here in chains,

01:17:15.250 --> 01:17:17.410
and the 10th Legion brought out within six months.

01:17:18.030 --> 01:17:20.410
I was in the council chamber. I heard the promise.

01:17:23.500 --> 01:17:25.980
Look, you may not realize this,

01:17:26.430 --> 01:17:28.250
but I've been buying time for both of us.

01:17:30.000 --> 01:17:32.200
My name heads a list and your name is on it.

01:17:32.600 --> 01:17:35.180
So if I take that little leap off the tarpe and rock,

01:17:35.990 --> 01:17:38.620
I won't be doing it alone. Understood?

01:17:39.420 --> 01:17:39.780
Understood.

01:17:42.250 --> 01:17:43.930
You'd better get yourself a new second in command.

01:17:46.590 --> 01:17:48.510
That's right. The one you've got is a spy for the opposition.

01:17:50.880 --> 01:17:51.240
Quadratus.

01:17:51.700 --> 01:17:53.480
And one other. What's his name?

01:17:54.120 --> 01:17:55.400
Morovius, your senior tribute.

01:17:58.240 --> 01:17:59.540
This has turned into quite an evening.

01:18:00.090 --> 01:18:03.000
And who is yours, Caesar? Find out for yourself.

01:18:04.790 --> 01:18:06.170
Oh, it's nobody you need be afraid of.

01:18:08.590 --> 01:18:09.790
Oh, look, it's not so bad.

01:18:10.770 --> 01:18:14.980
Once the troops are out of there, you can open the government palace at Caesarea,

01:18:15.300 --> 01:18:18.070
sit on the throne, make some laws, be visible.

01:18:19.030 --> 01:18:20.970
You'll be a very rich man in a very short time.

01:18:27.020 --> 01:18:29.640
You may not be aware of it, but this is your new...

01:18:30.220 --> 01:18:47.770
emblem of office i'm not ungrateful caesar it's just that i'm so tired you know it's uh hard to

01:18:47.770 --> 01:18:55.360
recognize you without a drink in your hand you'll be welcome all this we never said how sorry we all

01:18:55.360 --> 01:18:57.850
were to your lady i mean thank you

01:19:00.410 --> 01:19:04.410
It's not just tiredness. You really did expect those concessions to be granted, didn't you?

01:19:04.550 --> 01:19:06.800
Yes, I did, because it was a way of reason.

01:19:08.020 --> 01:19:11.040
It's unfortunate. Nobody regrets it more than I do,

01:19:11.160 --> 01:19:14.180
and sometimes reason can be treacherous.

01:19:15.110 --> 01:19:20.090
Caesar, when you and Titus and I were serving together in the field,

01:19:20.210 --> 01:19:23.650
we talked of one thing over and over again, a dream we had.

01:19:23.810 --> 01:19:27.860
It wasn't just a world without Nero, it was a world enlightened, was the way we put it.

01:19:28.330 --> 01:19:29.970
A gift Rome had to give the world.

01:19:30.000 --> 01:19:32.160
a way of life, civilization, peace.

01:19:33.090 --> 01:19:33.610
I remember.

01:19:34.160 --> 01:19:36.120
Do you remember this? Because it was you who said it.

01:19:37.350 --> 01:19:40.690
Without that dream as a mission, we were worse than the barbarians we conquered

01:19:40.690 --> 01:19:43.270
because they made no pretence of a desire for anything better.

01:19:43.410 --> 01:19:44.330
They had no dream.

01:19:47.300 --> 01:19:48.900
I think of the zealot and what I said to him,

01:19:50.000 --> 01:19:52.120
that we were better at building than at tearing down.

01:19:53.070 --> 01:19:56.780
I believed it when I said it, and I believed the dream to be a good one.

01:19:57.920 --> 01:19:58.920
Do you still believe it?

01:19:59.080 --> 01:19:59.880
More than ever before.

01:20:00.160 --> 01:20:04.950
I haven't changed. Look at me. I haven't changed.

01:20:06.970 --> 01:20:10.860
Lucianus, although he's a skilful man as well as an ambitious one,

01:20:10.900 --> 01:20:12.360
has never dreamed that dream and he never will.

01:20:14.050 --> 01:20:17.060
That is why, if what we all want is to be brought about,

01:20:18.330 --> 01:20:20.610
we have no choice now in Judea.

01:20:25.130 --> 01:20:28.170
About my second in command, I pray it won't come to this,

01:20:28.270 --> 01:20:29.970
but I may need a good siege command.

01:20:30.000 --> 01:20:31.860
Is Rubius Galla still alive?

01:20:32.020 --> 01:20:33.640
Yes, he is. He's yours. Good choice.

01:20:35.480 --> 01:20:37.360
What do I do about Quadratus and his friend?

01:20:38.840 --> 01:20:40.240
Whatever you like, as long as you're discreet.

01:20:40.960 --> 01:20:44.450
To success. To the dream.

01:20:47.120 --> 01:20:48.500
Happy birthday, Caesar.

01:21:18.270 --> 01:21:22.360
What do they expect us to do about it? Dance on the housetops?

01:21:23.620 --> 01:21:25.320
Let's pray they pass us by.

01:21:25.520 --> 01:21:29.920
We lost a father and three brothers when they celebrated Caligula's birth.

01:21:30.000 --> 01:21:56.960
Did they pass?

01:21:57.500 --> 01:21:57.760
Hello?

01:22:00.220 --> 01:22:01.480
Are you afraid for your daughter?

01:22:01.970 --> 01:22:03.550
For your wife, Matthias.

01:22:03.730 --> 01:22:06.700
Go back inside.

01:22:06.880 --> 01:22:07.180
No!

01:22:09.050 --> 01:22:10.770
She's used to the company of men.

01:22:15.020 --> 01:22:15.200
Hey!

01:22:17.020 --> 01:22:17.200
Hey!

01:22:30.440 --> 01:22:33.290
Alexandria needs to go dressed as a bride.

01:22:34.110 --> 01:22:34.950
You want a woman?

01:22:36.510 --> 01:22:37.400
I think I...

01:22:42.350 --> 01:22:46.010
I'm sorry, but then you never asked me who I wanted.

01:22:47.490 --> 01:22:58.510
Way to make a living.

01:22:58.710 --> 01:22:59.770
What? Peddling your wife.

01:23:00.000 --> 01:23:03.180
No, you clod. I mean the threshing floor over there.

01:23:03.720 --> 01:23:05.440
Farmers come from miles away.

01:23:05.850 --> 01:23:08.650
Probably pay six or eight track miles a bushel.

01:23:09.070 --> 01:23:10.110
I've seen it.

01:23:10.210 --> 01:23:10.870
So what?

01:23:11.070 --> 01:23:13.810
So a man could be very comfortable doing that for a living.

01:23:14.730 --> 01:23:17.190
Got anything better waiting for you back at home?

01:23:17.370 --> 01:23:18.320
No. No.

01:23:19.010 --> 01:23:21.730
We'll talk to the decorian about it as soon as we stop.

01:23:22.240 --> 01:23:25.560
If we ever stop, the man never seems to relieve himself.

01:23:25.900 --> 01:23:27.100
Only when he sleeps.

01:23:30.060 --> 01:23:30.980
Are you going to do it?

01:23:32.640 --> 01:23:34.020
I'm thinking about it.

01:23:34.640 --> 01:23:35.940
There's not much time.

01:23:36.730 --> 01:23:38.050
We get mustard out tomorrow.

01:23:40.200 --> 01:23:40.760
No, I don't.

01:23:41.590 --> 01:23:42.590
I've got another year.

01:23:43.890 --> 01:23:46.170
Besides, you know what I'd have to do if I want to talk to the General?

01:23:46.350 --> 01:23:48.840
I have to shave.

01:23:50.820 --> 01:23:51.840
Now, find somebody else.

01:23:52.090 --> 01:23:54.550
Nobody can talk for us but our own decorium.

01:23:56.840 --> 01:23:57.960
Stupid regulation, isn't it?

01:23:59.200 --> 01:23:59.960
I know what he wants.

01:24:00.090 --> 01:24:04.350
You want in, don't you? You're in.

01:24:09.360 --> 01:24:10.680
Chummy, sir!

01:24:11.550 --> 01:24:15.400
Sir, this request is made through channels and comes from two 20-year veterans.

01:24:15.850 --> 01:24:17.530
I asked the commander to consider it seriously.

01:24:18.110 --> 01:24:20.590
They don't expect mustering out pay on top of it, will they?

01:24:20.750 --> 01:24:22.330
Sir, they beg me to convey their best...

01:24:22.330 --> 01:24:24.490
Pretend you're a man, Dicurian, and talk like one?

01:24:24.960 --> 01:24:29.500
Sir, they'd be willing to take title to the property instead of the cash they've got coming.

01:24:31.720 --> 01:24:32.580
I don't doubt they would.

01:24:34.640 --> 01:24:35.620
Tell them I'm thinking about it.

01:24:35.800 --> 01:24:36.200
Yes, sir.

01:24:36.740 --> 01:24:37.140
Thank you, sir.

01:24:38.230 --> 01:24:41.310
Oh, de Curien, how much are you in for?

01:24:41.730 --> 01:24:42.990
A minusment is one year to go, sir.

01:24:45.500 --> 01:24:46.080
One-third, sir.

01:24:49.220 --> 01:24:49.500
Dismissed.

01:25:00.000 --> 01:25:08.050
not really thinking about it. Yes. What do we do about the others? In the next month, we'll have

01:25:08.050 --> 01:25:13.990
900 men mustering out. Precisely. And let's say that half of them decide to do the same as these

01:25:13.990 --> 01:25:21.350
three. That threshing floor alone could take 30 of them. Then there are orchards, olive presses,

01:25:22.070 --> 01:25:29.980
vineyards. Incredible opportunities. For an enterprising Roman? Yes, half of them.

01:25:30.000 --> 01:25:31.180
will probably jump at it.

01:25:32.120 --> 01:25:33.740
Whatever families they had

01:25:33.740 --> 01:25:35.400
are probably dead by now.

01:25:37.820 --> 01:25:38.840
Well, don't you see

01:25:39.860 --> 01:25:41.860
500 men signing over

01:25:41.860 --> 01:25:42.920
their mustering out pay

01:25:42.920 --> 01:25:45.010
of 500 drachmas each?

01:25:46.400 --> 01:25:48.440
I think we're moving too fast, sir.

01:25:49.180 --> 01:25:50.500
The land's not ours to give.

01:25:51.650 --> 01:25:52.570
In dispatches,

01:25:52.610 --> 01:25:53.270
we can call it

01:25:54.430 --> 01:25:56.330
reward for acts of bravery.

01:25:57.800 --> 01:25:58.580
During a truce.

01:26:00.640 --> 01:26:01.900
Oh, the Jews will have broken the truce.

01:26:03.430 --> 01:26:03.990
They will!

01:26:05.410 --> 01:26:05.810
Obvious.

01:26:06.970 --> 01:26:10.890
Two hundred and fifty thousand drachmas for us, to begin with.

01:26:12.890 --> 01:26:14.170
One day we'll be mustered out.

01:26:15.800 --> 01:26:17.680
I wish we'd had word from Lucianus.

01:26:18.650 --> 01:26:21.070
The next word from Lucianus will be short and sweet.

01:26:21.490 --> 01:26:23.770
We observe Vespasian's funeral.

01:26:25.040 --> 01:26:27.760
The Senate sends its best wishes and my commission.

01:26:28.830 --> 01:26:29.670
And the 10th...

01:26:30.380 --> 01:26:31.880
It clears its marching waters.

01:26:32.160 --> 01:26:40.840
If the savages haven't broken the truce by then, that ought to do it.

01:27:27.100 --> 01:27:29.690
Get this through your heads! This was our idea!

01:27:30.380 --> 01:27:31.160
We give the orders.

01:27:31.420 --> 01:27:34.040
I'm waiting for the day you try to give me an order.

01:27:35.340 --> 01:27:38.460
Now, who's going to live in that house?

01:28:00.700 --> 01:28:02.840
Not a centurion, darling. I'm a tribune.

01:28:03.260 --> 01:28:05.660
All the better, tribune. I am clean.

01:28:06.680 --> 01:28:07.200
Are you now?

01:28:07.670 --> 01:28:10.980
I was born in Egypt. I learned things in Egypt.

01:28:13.080 --> 01:28:13.520
Why me?

01:28:13.930 --> 01:28:16.800
It's obvious, tribune. You see the choice I have?

01:28:18.700 --> 01:28:21.110
Could give you to them afterwards.

01:28:22.280 --> 01:28:22.860
You won't.

01:28:25.160 --> 01:28:25.620
We'll see.

01:28:28.480 --> 01:28:29.700
My parents are in that house.

01:28:32.300 --> 01:28:46.600
It's all right! We're safe!

01:29:00.510 --> 01:29:06.350
They belong and valorous within the field of property.

01:29:25.490 --> 01:29:28.330
Caesar's name, this is your land.

01:29:41.350 --> 01:29:47.200
God will you see this and do nothing move them out all of them orders

01:29:50.590 --> 01:29:59.650
We'll have to vacate this settlement we must not stay in any case as soon as you set foot on our ground our ground became

01:30:00.000 --> 01:30:07.820
child there have been many caesars but none before dared to do this if you live long enough

01:30:07.820 --> 01:30:13.210
you'll see everything yes centurion you speak the truth

01:31:18.520 --> 01:31:19.800
Now then, what has brought you here?

01:31:21.180 --> 01:31:22.180
The truce has been broken.

01:31:22.340 --> 01:31:25.960
The Roman commander has seized all the farmland of the lower Jordan Valley.

01:31:33.580 --> 01:31:34.360
Has there been fighting?

01:31:35.250 --> 01:31:38.690
As always, when they move on us, they kill without question.

01:31:40.930 --> 01:31:42.450
Why are the Essene left alive?

01:31:42.980 --> 01:31:44.320
Because it pleases God.

01:31:46.740 --> 01:31:51.050
Why? Because he considers you holier than the rest of us?

01:31:51.810 --> 01:31:53.270
That you must ask him.

01:31:54.640 --> 01:31:59.480
The scrolls of the law and the prophets is now no safer place in Israel.

01:32:00.600 --> 01:32:02.280
You believe in this fortress now.

01:32:02.930 --> 01:32:04.550
Trolls must be kept safe.

01:32:04.960 --> 01:32:07.780
Then why not leave them here and go back down?

01:32:08.300 --> 01:32:10.280
We are the guardians of the written word.

01:32:10.360 --> 01:32:12.720
We may not be separated from it.

01:32:14.000 --> 01:32:14.480
Very convenient.

01:32:19.540 --> 01:32:21.700
You will now give ear to the spoken word.

01:32:21.880 --> 01:32:26.120
God has delivered you to a place of work.

01:32:26.940 --> 01:32:29.670
Work you will do as long as you are here.

01:32:30.670 --> 01:32:33.010
In a little time, this will be a place of war.

01:32:33.190 --> 01:32:35.920
Each of you will fight.

01:32:36.140 --> 01:32:39.240
Whoever will not work when he is bided to,

01:32:39.320 --> 01:32:41.780
whoever will not fight when the time comes,

01:32:41.860 --> 01:32:44.960
will be lifted up in these hands and thrown...

01:32:45.000 --> 01:32:49.450
down from this mountaintop and the scrolls after him.

01:32:49.820 --> 01:32:50.360
Elisa!

01:32:50.560 --> 01:32:56.130
With all due respect.

01:33:46.280 --> 01:33:54.150
seem to you. We have Vespasian's answer. Now let's give him ours.
